"explanation": "Ocean salinity is primarily derived from the weathering and erosion of continental rocks (eroding land), which releases ions into rivers that flow to the sea. Volcanic emissions (both subaerial and submarine) contribute soluble gases and minerals. Reactions on the sea floor, particularly at hydrothermal vents, leach metals and other ions from the oceanic crust. In contrast, glacial ice is formed from precipitation (fresh water) and contains negligible amounts of dissolved salts. When glacial ice melts, it adds fresh water to the ocean, which actually dilutes the salinity of the surrounding seawater rather than contributing to the salt content.",
